                <pb facs="0421" n="313" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg313"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 12 in No. 910.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Extract from minutes of proceedings of a court held on
                        July 15, 1892, on board Her Majesty’s ship Royalist, at Tarawa Island, for
                        the trial of Eno, a native of Raratonga.</hi></head>
                <p>4. For that he, the said Eno, did burn down the house of Jacob, a native of
                    Tarawa.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>He admitted the truth of the charges, but said * * * with reference to fourth
                    charge, he was ordered to do it by Kustel.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ed. H. M. Davis</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Captain.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
